{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/987239-syndicate-and-various-supernaturals","id":987239,"title":"Syndicate and various supernaturals","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-14T07:07:37-07:00","id":987239,"title":"Syndicate and various supernaturals","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In spite of the Void Engineer\u2019s reports, there are no such things as ghosts, faeries, demons, etc. They serve as entertaining (and profitable) fiction, nothing more. Now,<br /> in the laughable event that credible proof comes to light, that would be another matter. Some Financiers have written various marketing plans just in case, usually as a test by a higher-up to see what they can do when given completely ridiculous parameters. </div> </div> </div>Does that quote mean the Syndicate don't know and can't see ghosts, faeries, demons, etc or whilst they can see them and know something ghosts, faeries, demons, etc. like exist, but deem them as scientifically-comprehensible creatures, not some supernatural, mystical, unknowable phenomenon?<br /> <br /> Because, well, they are obviously able to see VE-provided &quot;evidences&quot; and have to deal with ghosts and faeries on occasions - certainly, if need arises.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","name":"Numinous","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T07:41:20-07:00","id":987251,"title":"","content":"Outside of the Main Supernatural Splats, i.E. Mages, Shifters and Vampires, the Union actually has only miniscule knowledge and incidents with the other supernaturals.<br /> <br /> The exception is the Void Engineers pretty much, be it Necronauts, their 'Ghostbusters' division or those out and about in the Umbra.<br /> The other Conventions are rather sceptic, and/or simply don't have those splats on their radar.<br /> The Convention that would be in second place are the Progenitors. Their Damage Control division might encounter those strange creatures on their missions, but you won't find them labeled as 'Fairies' or 'Demons' in their documents.<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> That said, I presume the Syndicate, going by the paste, knows that there are weird fairy-like and demon-like creatures out there, but simply refuses to literally label and acknowledge them as such - yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 10-14-2016, 10:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T09:09:51-07:00","id":987289,"title":"","content":"Guess it doesn't matter whether or not they know about them (and they probably do).<br /> <br /> It's just that mysticism and supernatural is bad for business. Those who know they are supernatural keep quiet about it and deflect the subject with controlled censure, and those who don't know they're supernatural just rationalize them with half-baked explanations (probably what I would've done).<br /> <br /> Note that even organizations on other splats do the same. Some truths are best kept hidden in the basement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T13:08:20-07:00","id":987395,"title":"","content":"It seems like a strange statement, because VE's don't believe in those things either. They believe in extradimensional aliens that the masses has often mistook for ghosts and demons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T18:04:45-07:00","id":987520,"title":"","content":"If I remember correctly, Iteration X began to look into extra-dimensional beings in their Revised Convention book, following the loss of the Computer and the lift of the ban on learning Dimensional Science. Granted, this was years before the rest of the Revised Convension books were developed, so how much this fits with other material is debatable. If it's true, though, then that means Iteration X is aware of things like Post Life Entities, in some capacity.<br /> <br /> Then there's the Book of Madness, which states that, despite the Union's general dismissal of superstitionist claims, there are plenty of Technocrats that know of the existence of &quot;demons&quot; and the like. Mostly from personal experience. These individuals are usually assigned afterwards to continue dealing with the same unexplained phenomenon, both because they are the most experienced in fighting them, and as a means of isolating that information from the rest of the Union. Naturally, this leads to an X-Files situation, where Technocrats are stuck in departments and cases that make their colleagues not take them seriously.<br /> <br /> Still, when there are events that smack of &quot;extra-dimensional corruption&quot; (read: possession and infernalism), the Union has people to deal with it, one way or another. While the anti-superstitionist party line is all well and good, these beings whose natures are not yet understood by Science pose a tangible threat to the Technocracy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T18:35:48-07:00","id":988045,"title":"","content":"Actually, I ran a game a few months ago where a young $yndicate advertiser named Roger accidentally got the first rank of Dimensional Science during a &quot;stimulant&quot; fueled all-night creativity session. He started seeing mascots and commercials moving when they shouldn't be, talking to <i>him</i> trying to get him to buy cereal and skin lotion. Roger thought he was going crazy until he saw a Traditionalist doing spirit-work, then it all clicked.<br /> <br /> Desperate to prove to himself that he isn't crazy <i>or</i> a reality deviant, Roger developed a theory that these &quot;spirits&quot; are Jungian projections and products of mass association of certain characters with certain attributes (Wily Coyote is clever, Flo from Progressive is quirky/cute, Mickey Mouse is wholesome, etc.). He tried to use contract-hypereconomics to get the copyright on Pomona (Greek goddess of fruit) and essentially enslave this fading minor goddess into selling healthy superfruits and smoothies. They're not human, so its okay right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10653-omegaz","name":"OmegaZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10653_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T21:01:31-07:00","id":988106,"title":"","content":"It's not that the Syndicate can't see them in a literal sense, it's that they're not profitable -- or in any way on which the Syndicate can honestly capitalize. And, until such a time as they become such, the Syndicate resorts to the Technocratic Union party line -- denialism. Were more Syndicate members well-versed in DimSci, and with the OPP Revised edition and M20 material there's certainly reason for more to become such given their warming relations with the VE's in the face of NWO opposition, they'd be a lock for getting involved in the Shadowlands in a <i>huge</i> way.<br /> <br /> You gotta remember that even in the case of the other fatsplats, the Syndicate's most-involved dealings with them are when they interfere with the Bottom Line. And, with the exception of vampires, dealings with which can prove <i>exceedingly</i> profitable, that's not generally on the friendliest of terms. Can't have Glass Walkers riling up techno-spirits to faf with social media connectivity, or other werewolves tearassing around ruining real estate values.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T09:44:06-07:00","id":988286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OmegaZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/987239-syndicate-and-various-supernaturals?p=988045#post988045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, I ran a game a few months ago where a young $yndicate advertiser named Roger accidentally got the first rank of Dimensional Science during a &quot;stimulant&quot; fueled all-night creativity session. He started seeing mascots and commercials moving when they shouldn't be, talking to <i>him</i> trying to get him to buy cereal and skin lotion. Roger thought he was going crazy until he saw a Traditionalist doing spirit-work, then it all clicked.<br /> <br /> Desperate to prove to himself that he isn't crazy <i>or</i> a reality deviant, Roger developed a theory that these &quot;spirits&quot; are Jungian projections and products of mass association of certain characters with certain attributes (Wily Coyote is clever, Flo from Progressive is quirky/cute, Mickey Mouse is wholesome, etc.). He tried to use contract-hypereconomics to get the copyright on Pomona (Greek goddess of fruit) and essentially enslave this fading minor goddess into selling healthy superfruits and smoothies. They're not human, so its okay right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not that the Syndicate has any problem with effective (and actual) slavery. At all. &quot;Human capital&quot;<br /> <br /> Roger might be in line for some re-education. His &quot;Dimensional Science&quot; is really full-on Spirit. He's acting like a Hermetic in pretty much every way with a few nods towards Dreamspeaker-ness He's obviously fully in acceptance of a &quot;place&quot; for extra-dimensional intrusion into mundane reality. And his handling of EDE's isn't just unorthodox, it's heretical/unmutual/whatever.<br /> <br /> Or... there might a Cultist out there who has used Time to set himself to be in the right place and right time for a little recruitment talk about Roger jumping ship for more enlightening drug-fueled brainstorming with the added benefit of keeping his mental integrity intact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1062,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","user":"Ajax","date":". 10-16-2016, 04:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T10:16:56-07:00","id":988297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/987239-syndicate-and-various-supernaturals?p=988286#post988286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not that the Syndicate has any problem with effective (and actual) slavery. At all. &quot;Human capital&quot;<br /> <br /> Roger might be in line for some re-education. His &quot;Dimensional Science&quot; is really full-on Spirit. He's acting like a Hermetic in pretty much every way with a few nods towards Dreamspeaker-ness He's obviously fully in acceptance of a &quot;place&quot; for extra-dimensional intrusion into mundane reality. And his handling of EDE's isn't just unorthodox, it's heretical/unmutual/whatever.<br /> <br /> Or... there might a Cultist out there who has used Time to set himself to be in the right place and right time for a little recruitment talk about jRoger umping ship for more enlightening drug-fueled brainstorming with the added benefit of keeping his mental integrity intact.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah, his bosses are watching him <i>very</i> closely. They're curious to see what happens and are shielding him from the rest of the Technocracy, but the moment he goes too far Enforcers are gonna shit in his cereal and turn him over to the NWO.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10653-omegaz","name":"OmegaZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10653_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T18:22:36-07:00","id":988550,"title":"","content":"On the original point: as I read it, the Technocracy party line is that ghosts and the like don't exist. And due to the NWO's conditioning policies, it's treasonous to say otherwise even if you know otherwise. As such, the quote from the book is an attempt to get around that fact, by treating the unspoken truth as if it were a hypothetical. That way, you can still address the issue without being sent to Room 101.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T18:44:15-07:00","id":988562,"title":"","content":"Well they have to acknowledge ghosts in some way, if for no other reason than they have dimension-traveling tech that can actually go there. It's fine if they want to pretend that ghosts are extradimensional aliens that have metamorphed into clones of human minds for some unknown reason, but not even acknowledging they exist in some form is ridiculous. That's like saying that the next town over doesn't exist when you can take a bus there for a dollar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T20:00:06-07:00","id":988631,"title":"","content":"I myself wrote a short description for a Spirit-using Syndicate rep, over in the 1001 Character Ideas thread. And I made a point of describing what he did as being extremely unmutual, and liable to get disciplinary action brought down if the Union ever found out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T11:23:01-07:00","id":988946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/987239-syndicate-and-various-supernaturals?p=988562#post988562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well they have to acknowledge ghosts in some way, if for no other reason than they have dimension-traveling tech that can actually go there. It's fine if they want to pretend that ghosts are extradimensional aliens that have metamorphed into clones of human minds for some unknown reason, but not even acknowledging they exist in some form is ridiculous. That's like saying that the next town over doesn't exist when you can take a bus there for a dollar.</div> </div> </div> </div>And the ludicrousness of the RAW partyline for the Union rears it's head yet again. &quot;We don't do magic. They don't do magic. There is no magic. There is no supernatural. There are no supernatural beings.&quot; When it's pretty obvious Technocrats do SOMETHING and it's pretty damn similar to what those guys call &quot;magic&quot;. If they don't do magic and there is no magic, then what are they doing? Apparently nothing, so they must not actually be problem. Same thing for vampires, changelings, wraiths, etc. They don't exist because they can't exist.<br /> <br /> There is solipsism and there is doublethink and then there is the kind of rank stupidity that goes way far past the &quot;non-functional&quot; line. Even if everyone KNOWS the party line is inane and wrong and circumvents it by playing word games (which have NO chance of working against the people who perfected that kind of thinking... utterly utterly transparent) it puts things past the point of farce.<br /> <br /> Meaning.... Ideologically, the Technocracy as written is too stupid and self-contradictory to exist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T18:00:26-07:00","id":989099,"title":"","content":"Frankly, this is a major reason behind my Skeptics hack. What if denial could be weaponized? Then the technocracy party line might actually make some sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T03:41:22-07:00","id":989279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/987239-syndicate-and-various-supernaturals?p=988946#post988946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the ludicrousness of the RAW partyline for the Union rears it's head yet again. &quot;We don't do magic. They don't do magic. There is no magic. There is no supernatural. There are no supernatural beings.&quot; When it's pretty obvious Technocrats do SOMETHING and it's pretty damn similar to what those guys call &quot;magic&quot;. If they don't do magic and there is no magic, then what are they doing? Apparently nothing, so they must not actually be problem. Same thing for vampires, changelings, wraiths, etc. They don't exist because they can't exist.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Mmmmh, I think the Technocracy Party Line actually works fine, if you think about it - the fallacy one needs to avoid is, that the Technocracy isn't actually going <i>'All those things out there do not exist! La La la!'</i><br /> <br /> If you think they are saying *that*, *literally*, then yes..their partyline makes no sense at all, because it would take a Technocratic field agent a week or two before they need to be shoveled back to Room 101.<br /> <br /> But That's not what they are actually doing or saying.<br /> <br /> What the Technocracy is saying, is <i>'All this strange stuff out there exists, yes. But it is not what all those supersticious people think it is. It is all clearly concepts that work within our Hyperscientific paradigm, It is all explainable. Stop it with the suspersticious &quot;Fairy&quot; stuff and mumbo-jumbo. We can explain this.'</i><br /> <br /> And this of course includes everything the Technocrats themselves manage to do. You do not need to believe that what you do is Magick, just because what you do is eerily similiar to what the people out there calling themselves 'Mages' do - it's <i>exactly the other way around</i>. &quot;Those other groups are clearly using principles of Hyperscience, psionics, field pyrokinetics etc. without realizing it, and they just won't accept that what they are dressing it as is absolute nonsense sillyness.&quot;<br /> <br /> And of *course* the Technocrats would believe that. They know what they can do. They know it's Enlightened Science and Hypertech. And when those weird guys out there are doing similiar things in a chaotic fashion, of *course* they must be using the same principles. They're just doing it in a delusional, wrong, hazardous and uncontrolled manner.<br /> <br /> So yes, their thoughts of '<i>We are not doing Magic, and neither are they.</i>' actually work within their worldview. And in a way, it's just as valid - it is simply the flipside view of '<i>We are doing Magick. And so are they!'</i> of the non-Technocrats. And each side wants to smack the other around with '<i>Don't you see what you are doing? Wake up!</i>'<br /> <br /> The difference between the Technocracy and the other Mages is, that while other Mages accept other paradigms with polite 'live and let live' ( while probably at first explaining things in their own paradigm in their mind ), that the Technocracy loudly, officially and strictly denies all non-Technocracy paradigms among their members. Everything out there is explainable through Technocratic Hyperscience and Tech. If the Technocracy can't explain it yet, they must do more tests and theories. And that's it. It's all covered.<br /> <br /> <br /> In short:<br /> <br /> It's not the belief in the existance of things out there that is against the partyline, it's <i>believing that those things aren't explainable through Technocratic paradigm</i> that causes the NWO to pay you a visit. If you start trying to explain those things outside the Technocratic paradigm, you are starting to lose faith in said paradigm's all-encompassing validity. And that's the line of thought they are trying to suppress. The Technocracy stands and falls with their members' faith (heh) in Hypertech and Enlightened Science.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 10-18-2016, 12:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T07:06:28-07:00","id":989328,"title":"","content":"I knew it!<br /> The Technos are Miracleworkers after all.\ud83d\ude1d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T09:47:25-07:00","id":989406,"title":"","content":"Well, the Technocracy also wants to reduce the probability of individual death due to supernatural causes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T11:42:12-07:00","id":989465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/987239-syndicate-and-various-supernaturals?p=989279#post989279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Mmmmh, I think the Technocracy Party Line actually works fine, if you think about it - the fallacy one needs to avoid is, that the Technocracy isn't actually going <i>'All those things out there do not exist! La La la!'</i><br /> <br /> If you think they are saying *that*, *literally*, then yes..their partyline makes no sense at all, because it would take a Technocratic field agent a week or two before they need to be shoveled back to Room 101.<br /> <br /> But That's not what they are actually doing or saying.<br /> <br /> What the Technocracy is saying, is <i>'All this strange stuff out there exists, yes. But it is not what all those supersticious people think it is. It is all clearly concepts that work within our Hyperscientific paradigm, It is all explainable. Stop it with the suspersticious &quot;Fairy&quot; stuff and mumbo-jumbo. We can explain this.'</i><br /> <br /> And this of course includes everything the Technocrats themselves manage to do. You do not need to believe that what you do is Magick, just because what you do is eerily similiar to what the people out there calling themselves 'Mages' do - it's <i>exactly the other way around</i>. &quot;Those other groups are clearly using principles of Hyperscience, psionics, field pyrokinetics etc. without realizing it, and they just won't accept that what they are dressing it as is absolute nonsense sillyness.&quot;<br /> <br /> And of *course* the Technocrats would believe that. They know what they can do. They know it's Enlightened Science and Hypertech. And when those weird guys out there are doing similiar things in a chaotic fashion, of *course* they must be using the same principles. They're just doing it in a delusional, wrong, hazardous and uncontrolled manner.<br /> <br /> So yes, their thoughts of '<i>We are not doing Magic, and neither are they.</i>' actually work within their worldview. And in a way, it's just as valid - it is simply the flipside view of '<i>We are doing Magick. And so are they!'</i> of the non-Technocrats. And each side wants to smack the other around with '<i>Don't you see what you are doing? Wake up!</i>'<br /> <br /> The difference between the Technocracy and the other Mages is, that while other Mages accept other paradigms with polite 'live and let live' ( while probably at first explaining things in their own paradigm in their mind ), that the Technocracy loudly, officially and strictly denies all non-Technocracy paradigms among their members. Everything out there is explainable through Technocratic Hyperscience and Tech. If the Technocracy can't explain it yet, they must do more tests and theories. And that's it. It's all covered.<br /> <br /> <br /> In short:<br /> <br /> It's not the belief in the existance of things out there that is against the partyline, it's <i>believing that those things aren't explainable through Technocratic paradigm</i> that causes the NWO to pay you a visit. If you start trying to explain those things outside the Technocratic paradigm, you are starting to lose faith in said paradigm's all-encompassing validity. And that's the line of thought they are trying to suppress. The Technocracy stands and falls with their members' faith (heh) in Hypertech and Enlightened Science.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that's not what the Technocracy party line is at all. You are making it sane and workable. Which is all the to the good, but it is quite clearly NOT what is stated in the game to be the case. Outright. With bells on. All sorts of crap dependent thereon. Like the getting in on the &quot;Big Secret&quot; after sufficient advancement. The same &quot;Big Secret&quot; that is completely obvious to even the most fanatical agent upon facing the enemy. The same &quot;Big Secret&quot; there is an entire institution (Room 101) dedicated to enforcing, even though it is completely unenforceable.<br /> <br /> I don't disagree with your position at all. It is one of many possible rationalizations that works much much MUCH better than the official stance in the game. But that's what the stance is. Official. The rest is Golden Ruling, which causes problems, because any Golden Rules changes need to be clearly labeled as such, since RAW is the fundamental basis on which this discourse is founded.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T01:12:19-07:00","id":989769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/987239-syndicate-and-various-supernaturals?p=989465#post989465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't disagree with your position at all. It is one of many possible rationalizations that works much much MUCH better than the official stance in the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>*Curtsies* Thank you! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/987239-syndicate-and-various-supernaturals?p=989465#post989465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except that's not what the Technocracy party line is at all. You are making it sane and workable. Which is all the to the good, but it is quite clearly NOT what is stated in the game to be the case. Outright. With bells on</div> </div> </div> </div>But..I really don't get the hardline-denial-of-everything feeling from the Technocracy books that have been released in the last years.<br /> <br /> I mean, let's go through a couple points in those:<br /> <br /> * The NWO Book introduces Atlas units, and has its whole Prologue and Epilogue dedicated to them - The Technocracy putting awakened Mage minds into cyborg bodies, *exactly* because they know that, just like them, the awakened Mages can work the same principles - they just need, ahem, guidance.<br /> Heck, the Prologue even has the interrogator describe the captured Mage as a 'Master of Forces'.<br /> <br /> * All books openly talk (in first person Technocracy-perspective) about 'Supernatural' beings like Vampires, Werewolves, Blood Magic etc.<br /> Heck, Hunters are called 'Mortals with supernatural powers'.<br /> Granted, folks like the Progenitors talk about about them in a more medical viewpoint, going for 'Homo Sapiens Mortis ' and such, but others talk about outright walking, dead bodies.<br /> <br /> * Even the old Iteration X revised book mentions that their combat Armatures recognize the enemy abilities as psionic manifestations, dimensional weirdness and 'unclassifiable phenomena', and that they 'recognize that the science of the Technocracy may be just one way of looking at things'.<br /> <br /> * The Guide To The Technocracy is all about 'We defend the world from the supernatural things in the dark'<br /> <br /> * The HDYDT Prologue has a Technocrat calmly and clinically accept something as normally spiritual as the concept of Reincarnation and ghost entities - simply because there is evidence for it:<br /> <br /> &quot;Studies indicate that sentience persists after<br /> physical death. In addition to the Post-Life<br /> Entities generated by unsettled manifestations<br /> of sentience, evidence suggests that consciousness<br /> reintegrates with physical stimuli in future<br /> incarnations. One does not have to be a mystic to<br /> accept such conclusions. The evidence supports them.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> The only hardline, unchanged, set-in-stone thing that I see that, yes, they try to pound into every Technocrat's head is 'We are doing Enlightened Science. We can do amazing things. NO THIS IS NOT MAGIC'.<br /> <br /> And as I described in my last post, that viewpoint works - based on their way of doing things.<br /> <br /> Now, I concede, maybe I am overlooking some writeups that fly right in the face of all that, but I don't think it's as black/white as you say it is written.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 10-19-2016, 04:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T11:14:39-07:00","id":989974,"title":"","content":"And the Technocracy clearly <i>knows </i>&quot;Enlightenment&quot; and &quot;Awakening&quot; is precisely same thing and says the Traditionalists are being &quot;Enlightened&quot;.<br /> <br /> So I wonder why the Syndicate acknowledges the Mages, the Vampires, the Werecreatures, Imbued, Umbrood, EDE and other weird supernatural but denies the Ghosts, Faeries and Demons and refer them &quot;other names&quot;.<br /> <br /> It has been outright mentioned that the Ghosts make havoc of Technocratic Constructs, research centers, and other Union-affiliated high tech facilities. So the Syndics have to see, or suffer, activities of the Ghosts. At least once in a life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","user":"Numinous","date":". 10-19-2016, 02:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","name":"Numinous","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T14:05:13-07:00","id":990091,"title":"","content":"And yet.... The party is still EXACTLY the &quot;head in the scientific sand&quot; idea. Even though it's contradicted elsewhere, because, well, it HAS to be. Since the Union is non-functional in a world where belief may determine reality but non-belief doesn't un-determine reality in the short term. Technocract agents who are not yet privy to the knowledge that magic is magic is magic is reality alteration by any other name cannot shield themselves from a vampires fangs, a werewolf's claws or a wraith's possession by denying their existence. They can't make a Hermetic's fireballs or a VA's reality hack go away in a poof of scientific logic. <br /> <br /> Which is why the internal contradiction between the reality of functionality in a world with magic vs. a denial of same is irreconcilable. And attempting to throw up the doublethink of Room 101 and the doctrine of unmutualness when denial won't work doesn't help. It makes things even worse. <br /> <br /> Ambrosia's way is better. Similarly, the way the Laundry feels about non-computational sorcerers in the series of the same name works as a decent rationalization. But what's in place? Nope. It's just silly. <br /> <br /> And, like so much else, it's going to stay that way due to inertia within the game's conceptualizations. New ideas about fundamentals just aren't something that is done with White Wolf games. What has been is and always shall be. Heaven help us all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T14:38:40-07:00","id":990103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Numinous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/987239-syndicate-and-various-supernaturals#post987239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does that quote mean the Syndicate don't know and can't see ghosts, faeries, demons, etc or whilst they can see them and know something ghosts, faeries, demons, etc. like exist, but deem them as scientifically-comprehensible creatures, not some supernatural, mystical, unknowable phenomenon?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's the party line - the section is a paraphrase of an official memo from the previous Synd book:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Previous ConvBook</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Board finds no evidence that these creatures exist, despite the claims of our Unionist colleagues. Even if these creatures were proven to exist, the Board can envision no possible scenario where their actions would have any derogatory effect on the Bottom Line. In short, grow up. There are no such things.</div> </div> </div> </div>(At the time this would have reflected both the Syndicate's disinterest in these things and some backroom SPD maneuvering - they wouldn't want anyone taking a look at their business partners with Spirit-enhanced equipment, after all. )<br /> <br /> Like all party lines, it reflects a basic sentiment (the VAs don't believe in ghosts either) but a given agent or someone with security clearance has a different picture of what's out there and what's possible. A syndic that encountered a spirit or ghost in the field would either understand it using known Union terminology (&quot;EDEs? I thought they were a VE prank!&quot;) or produce a suitable model within their paradigm (&quot;lingering psychological imprint upon the primal fabric&quot;), as that's just how paradigm works. Hell, you can unhaunt a haunted house by cleaning up its Resonance with Primal Utility (Flipping the house is just a form of exorcism, really) so that's not too far off from the truth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T16:54:37-07:00","id":990161,"title":"","content":"I imagine you would end up with an X-Files situation. Agents that believe in supernatural events would be given a basement office, but they would be tasked to deal with such phenomenon. If they capture or destroy the creature, they go back to the basement until the next incident. If they are killed, at least no one valuable died.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T19:25:51-07:00","id":990212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/987239-syndicate-and-various-supernaturals?p=990161#post990161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I imagine you would end up with an X-Files situation. Agents that believe in supernatural events would be given a basement office, but they would be tasked to deal with such phenomenon. If they capture or destroy the creature, they go back to the basement until the next incident. If they are killed, at least no one valuable died.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I said earlier in this very thread, this is exactly the case.<br /> <br /> From The Book of Madness, p. 81:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>What's A Demon Doing In My Enlightened Science?</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Many Technocrats and sympathizers fervently don't believe in the manifestations of the Infernal - they classify it with the same stuff as religion and &quot;magic&quot;. The experienced agents who come away with personal encounters with the paranormal may still be skeptical, and many continue to refuse to believe in demons and possession.<br /> The Technocracy leadership recognizes that an agent who's been exposed to the Infernal probably isn't quite the same afterward. As a result, agents who deal with the Infernal threats tend to find themselves stick in small amalgams and constantly assigned to similar cases - a sort of &quot;Infernal X-Files,&quot; if you will. These agents operate under a great deal of pressure and skepticism; their own divisions deride their reports, but the funding always seems to come in on time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just replace &quot;Infernal&quot; with &quot;Ghosts&quot;, and we're gold.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T20:05:24-07:00","id":990226,"title":"","content":"Of course, I think that it is much more likely for other supernatural to encounter Extraordinary Citizens rather than Enlightened Citizens. Extraordinary Citizens can be cool characters though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T03:41:48-07:00","id":991326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Union and the Syndicate have a lot of enemies: Traditionalists, Nephandi, vampires, werewolves, <b>Things From Beyond, </b>whatever the Void Engineers mean by \u201cThreat Null\u201d \u2014 the list goes on forever. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Other entities exist, but are even less common, including those known as \u201cdemons\u201d and \u201cmummies.\u201d Standard operating procedure: report and move off if benign. Flag to someone else (NWO Operatives, Progenitor Applies Sciences, <b>Syndicate Enforcers</b>, Traditionalists, \u201chunters,\u201d etc.) </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> With the younger or more rebellious of their kind, though, that\u2019s best left to other Conventions to exterminate. Not that we can\u2019t, but our Enforcers are<br /> better served <b>protecting the</b> <b>Bottom Line</b>. </div> </div> </div>...And I think Syndics are at least aware of demon-like, ghost-like and fairy-like beings exist and deal with(in other words; eradicate) them accordingly. It seems they just don't conceive they are <i>really </i>demons, faeries, etc. featured in various myths and legends. They merely don't take it literal sense as Reality Deviants.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","name":"Numinous","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T17:39:42-07:00","id":991620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Numinous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/987239-syndicate-and-various-supernaturals?p=991326#post991326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> ...And I think Syndics are at least aware of demon-like, ghost-like and fairy-like beings exist and deal with(in other words; eradicate) them accordingly. It seems they just don't conceive they are <i>really </i>demons, faeries, etc. featured in various myths and legends. They merely don't take it literal sense as Reality Deviants.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what I always assumed; that they, for example, think &quot;ghosts&quot; are extradimensional aliens that are either pretending to be ghosts, or have cloned human minds and thus genuinely believe themselves to be the deceased.<br /> <br /> But as several people in this thread have shown, at least some of the Technocrat material claims that they don't believe in ghosts in any form. A claim that should make any of their Dimensional Science people laugh out loud.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T19:52:15-07:00","id":993262,"title":"","content":"No, the Syndicate will call ghosts &quot;ghosts&quot; and changelings &quot;fairies&quot; because they believe propaganda-driven demands on speech are stupid. The Convention believes in following Sleeper culture and affirming whatever makes them happy. The insidious thing is that &quot;ghost&quot; is a *literally* meaningless to them outside of a brand or exploitable cultural designation. Things have names because Sleepers name them, and create cultural phenomena that can be exploited. So the terrifying shades of your ancestors become cartoons and cereal box mascots and the whole thing stops being believable, because the term &quot;ghost&quot; belongs to a consumer-driven hyper-reality with no substance worth paying attention to. If necessary the Syndicate treats ghosts as psychic phenomena and eliminates anything about them that &quot;damages the brand,&quot; but they don't really matter as *things.*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Writer, Game Designer, Pro since 99.<br /> <br /> Thoughts at <a href=\"http://mobunited.com\" target=\"_blank\">mobunited.com</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/164-malcolm","name":"Malcolm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T21:11:05-07:00","id":993299,"title":"","content":"The party line is that they don't believe in ghosts/demons/faeries/whatevers. They believe that there's things out there that are called that, but there are comprehensive scientific explanations for their existence, even if they hasn't been put together yet. Agents who deal with these things and persist in using superstitious modes of thinking to refer to them need to tighten their belts and get with proper modes of thought.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}